# p_9b2e — Standard split, dinner at eight, Priya wears her glasses (fork of p_a1b2)

Fork of p_a1b2. The core routine is unchanged: Elena commutes all five weekdays (8:00–17:30) taking laptop, backpack, wallet, hat, helmet, bike lock, and umbrella out of the house. Priya is home with a morning walk and afternoon errands. The dog is fed by Priya at 7:30 and walked by Elena at 18:00.

Two changes. First, the dinner window is shifted later: the resident sightings on Tuesday at 20:00 show Priya at the dining table and Elena in the kitchen, and the worst-object list shows glass_priya, plate_priya, and water_bottle_priya all at dining_table_d1 at 20:00. The old 18:30–20:00 window was too early; dinner is 19:30–21:00. Second, Priya's glasses are ON_PERSON from 7:00 to 22:00 (the empty look at the nightstand during 9–17 h is because she is wearing them, not because they are out of the house).

What sets this apart from p_4a7c: the helmet and bike lock go OUT_OF_HOUSE with Elena (she cycles), not stay at the entry. What would refute it: helmet_elena found at entry_hook_e1 at 12:00 on a weekday, or the dining table empty of plates at 20:00 on a Tuesday.

